    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308">

                <pb facs="0302" n="292" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/7–744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Representative to the Provisional Government
                        of the French Republic at Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Algiers</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-07T17:00:00+02:00">July 7, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:03 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2307. From Murphy. The CinC<anchor n="10" xml:id="d308-f1"/> has requested advice
                    at the instance of General Eaker<anchor n="11" xml:id="d308-f2"/> regarding the
                    status of the Republics of San Marino and Andorra and the Principalities of
                    Monaco and Liechtenstein. General Eaker is particularly desirous of knowing <pb
                        facs="0303" n="293" xml:id="pg293"/> whether German troops and matériel
                    passing through those states could be attacked from the air. Admiral
                        Cunningham<anchor n="12" xml:id="d308-f3"/> also points out that Monaco is
                    of capital importance because in addition to the port it is on the main road and
                    railroad from Italy to France. Department’s guidance is requested. [Murphy.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d308-f1" n="10" xml:id="d308-f1-content">
                <p>Commander in Chief, Gen. Dwight D. Eisenhower.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d308-f2" n="11" xml:id="d308-f2-content">
                <p>Lt. Gen. Ira C. Baker, U.S. Army, Air Commander in Chief of Mediterranean Allied
                    Air Force.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d308-f3" n="12" xml:id="d308-f3-content">
                <p>Adm. John Henry Dacres Cunningham, British Allied Naval Commander, Mediterranean
                    Theater.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
